# Drafted by Gemini (R18 gorthos), edited.

~ parley1
Narrator: On the stone altar, the gutted stag carcass turns its long skull toward you, a wet rattle rising from its split throat.
gorthos [neutral]: You are in the wood now. I have waited for your steps on the moss. Do not hurry. The rot has all the night it needs.
* Who are you? -> p1_who
* Why is the forest dying? -> p1_why
* Why let us walk here? -> p1_patience
* End this talk. -> p1_out

~ p1_who
gorthos [weary]: I was Farryn of the Greenwood, once, when the leaves were clean. I ate the old stag in the dark, and now I am Gorthos.
-> parley1

~ p1_why
gorthos [neutral]: The wood is not dying. It is softening so the old bark can fall away. Everything must rot down to black mould before the world starts green again.
-> parley1

~ p1_patience
gorthos [neutral]: My roots are deep in the wellspring, and my circle can only walk so far. I need warm lungs to carry my spores past the water.
set mem_farryn_circle
-> parley1

~ p1_out
gorthos [neutral]: Walk on through the spores. We will speak again when your bread turns grey.
set hb_parley1
-> END

~ parley2
Narrator: High in the carved beech, the half-eaten torso of Halden Wreath swings by its ribs, his slack jaw working around a thick grey tongue.
gorthos [neutral]: The Crooked Queen keeps this realm in cold bone and terror. I am her undoing. When the Emerald Rebirth takes her throne, the cruel winter ends.
* What do you want? -> p2_want
* What are the visions? -> p2_visions
* [if flag.hb_has_likeness] Gwenna? -> p2_gwenna
* End this talk. -> p2_out

~ p2_want
gorthos [weary]: I want the Green Queen back in the boughs. I want a quiet wood where the wolves do not tear what is gentle, and Gwenna walks beside me.
-> parley2

~ p2_visions
gorthos [sad]: The spring is full of what I was. My old thoughts spill over the stones and catch in the damp air like cobwebs.
set mem_farryn_gwenna
-> parley2

~ p2_gwenna
Narrator: The dead trapper's chest stops heaving, and the birch bark around the ropes creaks in the sudden quiet.
gorthos [afraid]: Put that away. That is her face before the teeth found her. It burns the back of my eyes to look at it.
-> parley2

~ p2_out
gorthos [neutral]: Come down to the heart when your breath grows heavy. The wellspring is waiting.
set hb_parley2
-> END

~ parley3
Narrator: Yellow foam bubbles from the split trunk of the fallen gloomwood, speaking in a slow, sodden sigh.
gorthos [weary]: You have walked farther than I thought your flesh could bear. Still, you breathe my air with every step.
* We are not carrying your blight anywhere. -> p3_refuse
* You do not care what dies in this forest. -> p3_care
* Leave it be. -> p3_out

~ p3_refuse
gorthos [neutral]: Refusing is only words. The spores are already in your wool and under your nails. You will carry me whether you wish it or not.
-> parley3

~ p3_care
gorthos [sad]: I care more than the Queen ever did. That is why the cruelty must rot out by the root, so nothing hurts like that again.
-> parley3

~ p3_out
gorthos [neutral]: Come to the den. There is very little left to say.
set hb_parley3
-> END

~ shadow
Narrator: Beyond the low red coals, a vast antlered shadow stands among the trunks, two pale eyes shining through the damp dark.
gorthos [sad]: Do not wake them yet, {name}. She used to laugh by firelight just like this. Praying to the Patient Lady did not save her from the teeth.
* Listen to her. -> shadow_listen
* Wake the others. -> shadow_wake

~ shadow_listen
gorthos [neutral]: Only the rot lasts long enough to mend a broken world. Let the mould into your marrow tonight, and it will lend you its strength.
* Take the bargain. -> shadow_take
* Refuse it. -> shadow_refuse

~ shadow_take
Narrator: A cold, sweet dampness settles into your chest, steady and heavy as wet earth.
set hb_shadow_bargain
set hb_blight += 1
inspiration
-> END

~ shadow_refuse
gorthos [weary]: Keep your dry bones a little longer, then. The morning will be no kinder.
-> END

~ shadow_wake
Narrator: By the time your hand touches a sleeping shoulder, the shining eyes have gone out, leaving only the smell of wet leaves.
-> END

~ den_arrive
Narrator: Bone charms and oozing fungal sacs hang from veins of black root. High on the far wall, the gaunt upper body of a young satyr juts from the pulsing rot.
quest q_hartsblight den
gorthos [weary]: You have come to the bottom of the wood. The air is thick here, is it not?
* Hear her out. -> den_plea
* [Perception DC 17] Search the torso. -> den_search | den_nothing
* Strike first. -> den_fight

~ den_search
Narrator: Behind the frail satyr ribs, the fungal wall heaves; her waist is fused into a colossal mass of stag bone and rotting timber hidden in the dark.
set hb_den_body_seen
-> den_arrive

~ den_nothing
Narrator: The yellow pus and tangled root-veins hide whatever holds her pinned against the stone.
-> den_arrive

~ den_plea
gorthos [neutral]: Thank you for ending Gwenna's pain in the water. Her strength has come home to me, though I am too heavy to leave this cave. Lie down in the mould, die gently, and rise to carry our Rebirth outward.
set hb_den_heard
* [if item:gwenna_sketch] Show her Gwenna's likeness. -> den_likeness
* Accept the Blight. -> den_accept
* Reject her. -> den_reject

~ den_likeness
Narrator: The gaunt satyr flinches back against the wet roots, her fingers curling in the slime.
gorthos [afraid]: Gwenna. No, do not look at me with her eyes. I did this so she would breathe again.
set hb_likeness_shown
set mem_farryn_gwenna
-> den_plea

~ den_accept
Narrator: Farryn's long, grey-barked finger reaches down from the wall, trembling and slick with spore-paste, waiting for one of you to touch it.
gorthos [neutral]: One touch is all it takes. The pain is shorter than a winter breath.
* I am sure. -> den_accept2
* No. -> den_plea

~ den_accept2
Narrator: The smell of sweet, spoiled water fills your nose; there is no coming back from this touch.
* Let it happen. -> den_accept3
* No. -> den_plea

~ den_accept3
sacrifice
if check.last
set hb_accepted_blight
Narrator: {name} drops into the soft grey moss without a sound, still and hollow, waiting not for a healer's hand, but for the beast itself to rise.
endif
-> den_plea

~ den_reject
cutscene hb_beast_revealed
Narrator: Up on the fungal wall, Farryn closes her eyes, and the wet tendons around her ribs draw tight.
cutscene hb_beast_revealed_2
Narrator: The cave wall tears open in a shower of black loam as a colossal stag of bone, blighted wood, and weeping fungus steps forward on cloven hooves.
cutscene end
gorthos [sad]: Then your bodies will feed the roots where they fall.
set hb_gorthos_started
combat hb_gorthos

~ den_fight
gorthos [weary]: So be it. The soil takes everything in the end.
set hb_gorthos_started
combat hb_gorthos

~ den_farewell
cutscene hb_gorthos_dies
Narrator: The towering stag buckles at the knees, its timber and bone running together into green, then brown, then a puddle of yellow sludge.
cutscene hb_gorthos_dies_2
Narrator: Pale motes lift from the mire and drift out of the cave mouth, riding the dark wind toward another province.
cutscene end
gorthos [sad]: Gwenna.
Narrator: A long, sour heat uncoils from your chests, and the rot goes out of your bodies like a breath finally let go.
set hb_blight = 0
set gorthos_slain
set fallen_farryn_dead
set mem_farryn_forest_love
quest q_hartsblight gorthos_destroyed
xp milestone
-> END
